# Environment / secrets
#
# `.env-default` holds DEFAULTS AND PLACEHOLDERS ONLY and is tracked; the actual
# configuration belongs in `.env`, which is never committed (IMPLEMENTATION.md
# §"Configuration"). `.env` used to be a tracked symlink to `.env-default`, so any
# real value written for local use — a service credential, a Redis password —
# landed straight in git. Copy the template instead:
#     cp .env-default .env
.env
.env.*
!.env-default
# ...but the placeholder templates are meant to be tracked.
!.env.example
!.env-default
